The position of '''Mandalorian Armorer'''<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> was held by a [[Mandalorian]] tasked with forging [[Mandalorian armor|armor]] and gear out of [[beskar]] metal.<ref name="Chapter 3" /> The Mandalorian method for forging beskar was a closely guarded secret, a skill passed on through generations to keep ancient armor intact and impervious.<ref name="Forge Databank">{{Databank|the-armorer-s-forge|The Armorer's forge}}</ref> One armorer, who was known simply as "[[the Armorer]]," was part [[the Tribe]] on [[Nevarro]] after the [[Great Purge of Mandalore]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> She kept the tradition of the Mandalorian people alive by forging beskar<ref name="The Armorer">{{Databank|the-armorer|the Armorer}}</ref> in a [[cryo-furnace]]. However, she also reminded the Tribe to never remove their [[helmet]]s in the presence of another, claiming this was the [[Way of the Mandalore]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> During the [[Clash on Nevarro]], after reminding him of [[Mandalorian Creed]], she tasked [[Din Djarin]] with bringing [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] to the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

